[[:db/retract 17592186172233 :question/answer-fields 17592186168261] {:db/id 17592186172132 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0c98998f-cfca-568f-8a23-cab1aa107bdb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172233 :question/problem "$$\n⟨\\text{_______}\\,,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\n$$\n\nThe fundamental vector product of the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [0,\\pi ]$ is given above. What is the $1$st component of the product?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,\\pi ].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,(x,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ and\n\n$$\nD={(x,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂x},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂x}⟩=⟨1,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨0,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f{f}^{′}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +f{f}^{′}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f{f}^{′},\\,-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ So, finally, we conclude that the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-247cda82-3b8b-57b4-bd85-1eaf3e646212"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-247cda82-3b8b-57b4-bd85-1eaf3e646212" :answer-field/id #uuid "247cda82-3b8b-57b4-bd85-1eaf3e646212" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c191f424-9120-5984-b367-462661abdf0f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e38d5fae-3d16-5915-8cda-f00c09b669d1" "answer-a106d988-56e8-55fb-9494-97df8b832cbd" "answer-c191f424-9120-5984-b367-462661abdf0f" "answer-dcf41d2a-2802-588f-84c7-9bab46e26c74" "answer-74de9016-aec8-5c6f-9c78-665b929a97ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e38d5fae-3d16-5915-8cda-f00c09b669d1" :answer/id #uuid "e38d5fae-3d16-5915-8cda-f00c09b669d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a106d988-56e8-55fb-9494-97df8b832cbd" :answer/id #uuid "a106d988-56e8-55fb-9494-97df8b832cbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c191f424-9120-5984-b367-462661abdf0f" :answer/id #uuid "c191f424-9120-5984-b367-462661abdf0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcf41d2a-2802-588f-84c7-9bab46e26c74" :answer/id #uuid "dcf41d2a-2802-588f-84c7-9bab46e26c74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74de9016-aec8-5c6f-9c78-665b929a97ce" :answer/id #uuid "74de9016-aec8-5c6f-9c78-665b929a97ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172056 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a20cac79-e438-5720-941d-255bfdc76ec3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a20cac79-e438-5720-941d-255bfdc76ec3" :question/id #uuid "a20cac79-e438-5720-941d-255bfdc76ec3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161037" :question/problem "$$\nr(z,\\theta )=⟨\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\text{__________},\\,z⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(z,\\theta )$ above parametrizes the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $x=\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}$ by  $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis for $z\\in [1,5].$ What is the second  component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/d3/d3302b5f4ea4c0387d70ac8f78e03e486fff9579f1a6b5e5cec08a31cde76af3.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $x=f(z)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $x=f(z)=\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [1,5].$   \n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(z,\\theta )=⟨\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,z\\in [1,5],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $r$ is $\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-638d8ce0-aca0-5ff6-85a7-9e3d7a370c18"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-638d8ce0-aca0-5ff6-85a7-9e3d7a370c18" :answer-field/id #uuid "638d8ce0-aca0-5ff6-85a7-9e3d7a370c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0244fab1-dcd6-5c87-8769-552570471608" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f50a75f-3d11-54f7-b72f-ea3bd8cf01f5" "answer-645d906f-848f-5e5e-92cb-479ed4f50490" "answer-5ceeb26c-796b-593b-80a8-390a78233aa1" "answer-0244fab1-dcd6-5c87-8769-552570471608" "answer-aa5125a1-4c8d-52e7-9aac-67e23cb420b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f50a75f-3d11-54f7-b72f-ea3bd8cf01f5" :answer/id #uuid "5f50a75f-3d11-54f7-b72f-ea3bd8cf01f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-645d906f-848f-5e5e-92cb-479ed4f50490" :answer/id #uuid "645d906f-848f-5e5e-92cb-479ed4f50490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ceeb26c-796b-593b-80a8-390a78233aa1" :answer/id #uuid "5ceeb26c-796b-593b-80a8-390a78233aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1-{z}^{2}}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0244fab1-dcd6-5c87-8769-552570471608" :answer/id #uuid "0244fab1-dcd6-5c87-8769-552570471608" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa5125a1-4c8d-52e7-9aac-67e23cb420b7" :answer/id #uuid "aa5125a1-4c8d-52e7-9aac-67e23cb420b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{z}^{2}-1}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0c98998f-cfca-568f-8a23-cab1aa107bdb" :question/id #uuid "0c98998f-cfca-568f-8a23-cab1aa107bdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161060" :question/problem "$$\n⟨\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\,,\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,,\\,\\text{_______}⟩\n$$\n\n \n\nThe fundamental vector product of the surface of revolution generated by rotating the curve $y=\\sqrt{z-1}$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $z$-axis for $z\\in [1,10]$ is given above. What is the $3$rd component of the product?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $y=\\sqrt{z-1}\\ge 0$ for all $z\\in [1,10].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(z)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,f(z)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩,\\,(z,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(z)=\\sqrt{z-1},$ and  \n\n$$\nD={(z,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 10,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂z},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂z}⟩=⟨{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-{f}^{′}f{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -{f}^{′}f{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-{f}^{′}f⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\sqrt{z-1},$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z-1}}.$ So, finally, we conclude that the fundamental vector product is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}=⟨\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\sqrt{z-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f2a4e677-4714-5cf2-98da-8e4b0964eb3f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f2a4e677-4714-5cf2-98da-8e4b0964eb3f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a4e677-4714-5cf2-98da-8e4b0964eb3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79004dcb-4e5d-5f5d-8fa0-3bf03f93e5ca" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41b7e536-caa1-5770-93ef-a558a35bf097" "answer-79004dcb-4e5d-5f5d-8fa0-3bf03f93e5ca" "answer-0a05c2e1-fb8c-50d3-b809-4010efe33716" "answer-da7f796f-a386-5f76-a134-0786b69fca45" "answer-5238fd8c-d50c-56c0-a63c-162bd3f52406"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41b7e536-caa1-5770-93ef-a558a35bf097" :answer/id #uuid "41b7e536-caa1-5770-93ef-a558a35bf097" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{(z-1)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79004dcb-4e5d-5f5d-8fa0-3bf03f93e5ca" :answer/id #uuid "79004dcb-4e5d-5f5d-8fa0-3bf03f93e5ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a05c2e1-fb8c-50d3-b809-4010efe33716" :answer/id #uuid "0a05c2e1-fb8c-50d3-b809-4010efe33716" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{(z-1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da7f796f-a386-5f76-a134-0786b69fca45" :answer/id #uuid "da7f796f-a386-5f76-a134-0786b69fca45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{z-1}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5238fd8c-d50c-56c0-a63c-162bd3f52406" :answer/id #uuid "5238fd8c-d50c-56c0-a63c-162bd3f52406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{z-1}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172133 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b858f50b-1a14-576c-973e-c7199e8e8cdb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-b858f50b-1a14-576c-973e-c7199e8e8cdb" :question/id #uuid "b858f50b-1a14-576c-973e-c7199e8e8cdb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161090" :question/problem "Use a fundamental vector product to determine which of the following integrals gives the surface area generated when the curve $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})$ is rotated by $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis for $y\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\ge 0$ for all $y\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ The parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨f(y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y,\\,f(y)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,(y,\\theta )\\in D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2}),$ and\n\n$$\nD={(y,\\theta )\\,:\\,-\\pi \\le y\\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂y},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂y}\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂y}⟩=⟨{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,1,\\,{f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂\\theta },\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂\\theta }⟩=⟨-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0,\\,f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0 & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & {f}^{′}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 1 \\\\ -f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f{f}^{′}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -f{f}^{′}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\,f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-f{f}^{′},\\,f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-f{f}^{′})^{2}+(f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{y}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2}),$ we obtain ${f}^{′}(y)=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2}).$ So, finally, we conclude that our expression for the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2}))}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-47b1c789-64a3-55f5-9e7d-ac42dc183f0e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-47b1c789-64a3-55f5-9e7d-ac42dc183f0e" :answer-field/id #uuid "47b1c789-64a3-55f5-9e7d-ac42dc183f0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4ddf6f00-c938-50e9-9408-30046a58b1f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ddf6f00-c938-50e9-9408-30046a58b1f1" "answer-6426d8d3-9d04-5e0f-a517-240093a9074a" "answer-1a49bca9-5ff7-58a4-97d5-3b205c07eee8" "answer-8a136f45-dabb-5965-b74e-f1e60e2efbab" "answer-066318d7-b3c3-582b-8704-baaa946c3602"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ddf6f00-c938-50e9-9408-30046a58b1f1" :answer/id #uuid "4ddf6f00-c938-50e9-9408-30046a58b1f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6426d8d3-9d04-5e0f-a517-240093a9074a" :answer/id #uuid "6426d8d3-9d04-5e0f-a517-240093a9074a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a49bca9-5ff7-58a4-97d5-3b205c07eee8" :answer/id #uuid "1a49bca9-5ff7-58a4-97d5-3b205c07eee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{y}{2})}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8a136f45-dabb-5965-b74e-f1e60e2efbab" :answer/id #uuid "8a136f45-dabb-5965-b74e-f1e60e2efbab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{y}